 {"complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-04T15:23:08.617291Z", "id": "RELEASE-007", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-04 on the published v1.1.0 wheel (sha256 f50fff23) in a fresh python3.14 venv: pip install --no-deps rc=0, dist metadata version 1.1.0 correct, but top_level.txt lists __init__, core, dashboard, db, debug_screen, env_service, game_loop, main, memory_reader, observability, ptp_cli, schemas, simple_test, test_all_roms, test_pyboy, vision — i.e. the contents of src/ were installed at site-packages ROOT instead of under a src/ package. Consequences: import src fails (importlib.util.find_spec(\"src\") is None) so every documented AGENTS.md invocation of the form python -m src.game_loop fails from an installed wheel; no entry_points.txt / console script is declared; site-packages is polluted with a bare __init__.py plus generic names (core, main, db) that can collide with other distributions. Root cause: pyproject.toml declares [project] name/version but no [tool.setuptools] package-dir/packages mapping, while the code lives in src/. The sdist keeps the correct src/ layout. Same shape shipped in v1.0.0 (asset ptp_01x_pokemon_ai-1.0.0-py3-none-any.whl), so this is a carried-forward artifact gap, recorded in the v1.1.0 release notes Known issues and not a regression of this cut. Publishing nothing: closing this row requires a packaging change plus a rebuilt artifact, which is foreman work.", "status": "complete", "title": "P1 — published wheel is not a usable package: src/* flattened into site-packages root, no entry point, documented 'python -m src.game_loop' fails from the installed artifact (affects v1.0.0 and v1.1.0)", "acceptance_criteria": "1) pyproject.toml declares an explicit setuptools package mapping for the src/ tree ([tool.setuptools] package-dir plus packages, or equivalent), and a fresh python -m build from the tagged tree produces a wheel whose file list has NO module or package at site-packages root other than the real distribution packages (no bare __init__.py, no top-level core/, main.py, game_loop.py). 2) In a clean venv, pip install --no-deps of that wheel then runs the documented entry path successfully: the documented invocation (python -m src.game_loop --help, or the replacement command the change documents in AGENTS.md/README) exits 0 without the repo checkout on sys.path. 3) If the import root is intentionally changed, AGENTS.md/README/docs examples are updated in the same commit and scripts/release_check.py still exits 0. 4) Row closes with the wheel file list, the clean-venv command transcript, the new asset sha256, and green CI at the committing SHA.", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T14:37:15-05:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "834f10a31575528f9b2ccf2ca3501673cdf6bfb2f53fd52719e8f27c15303c0a"}, "foreman_note": "releng sweep ai-plays-poke-releng-2026-11-04-14-55-04 (2026-11-04): defect RE-PROVEN LIVE at HEAD a6ca517 by independent local rebuild, not inherited from the prior tick's measurement. Evidence: uv build --wheel . rc=0 produced ptp_01x_pokemon_ai-1.1.0-py3-none-any.whl (360034 bytes); unzip -l top-level entries = core/ dashboard/ db/ observability/ ptp_cli/ schemas/ vision/ plus bare __init__.py game_loop.py main.py memory_reader.py env_service.py debug_screen.py simple_test.py test_all_roms.py test_pyboy.py generate_yellow_screenshots.py at site-packages ROOT; dist-info carries METADATA/WHEEL/top_level.txt/RECORD only, NO entry_points.txt. Root cause confirmed at the manifest: pyproject.toml has a [build-system] block (setuptools>=61.0, wheel) and no [tool.setuptools] section at all, so no package-dir/packages mapping exists for the src/ tree. Priority raised P2 to P1 because the defect ships in every published artifact (v1.0.0 and v1.1.0) and makes the documented invocation unusable from a clean install. Dispatch ladder, in order: (1) add [tool.setuptools] package-dir {'' = 'src'} plus packages = ['...'] enumerating the real packages (or find_namespace_packages), and optionally [project.scripts] for the CLI; (2) rebuild a wheel and prove the file list has no module/package at site-packages root other than the real distribution packages; (3) clean venv pip install --no-deps then run the documented entry path without the repo on sys.path; (4) if the import root changes, update AGENTS.md/README in the same commit and keep scripts/release_check.py at rc=0. Release consequence: once this lands as a fix commit, releng will cut v1.1.1 as a patch (Decision 1 rule 5) to publish a working artifact; until then no cut is due (R3). Do not hand-edit the published v1.1.0 assets.\n\n[landed 2026-11-04 70c272b] Defect closed by 70c272b (CI 41895641618 success, gitreins tier1 PASS, failover tier2 PASS 3e38f554). Wheel top-level is now src/ + dist-info only; clean py3.13 --no-deps install runs `python -m src.game_loop --help` rc 0 outside the checkout. The 402 tier2 verdict eb5df5a8 is an unfunded-provider artifact, not a rejection. Releng: v1.1.1 patch cut is due.", "completed_at": "2026-11-04T14:37:15-05:00", "branch": "main", "worktree": "/home/kara/ai_plays_poke", "primary_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "primary_provider": "openai-codex", "worker_status": "died_mid_guarded_commit_foreman_completed", "guard_result": "foreman-verified: pytest tests/ -q -m 'not heavy' => 4539 passed, 8 skipped, 62 deselected (rc 0); focused tests/test_integration.py+test_goap.py+ptp_cli+test_game_loop.py+test_packaging.py => 366 passed; ruff check clean; mypy clean; wheel build rc 0 top-level = src/ + dist-info only; clean py3.13 --no-deps install + python -m src.game_loop --help rc 0 outside the checkout; scripts/release_check.py rc 0 (5/5 PASS); gitreins tier1 PASS (lint+secrets+tests)", "ci_result": "success", "worker_summary": "RELEASE-007 landed as 70c272b. pyproject.toml gains [tool.setuptools] packages enumerating the real src tree (src + src.core/.dashboard/.db/.observability/.ptp_cli/.schemas/.vision) with include-package-data=false, so the wheel installs the src package itself instead of flattening its contents into site-packages. src/game_loop.py imports through src.* (three bare-root imports normalized), argparse moved into _build_parser() and evaluated from a guarded __main__ block before the heavy imports so --help works in a --no-deps install. tests/test_integration.py, tests/test_goap.py, tests/test_game_loop.py and tests/ptp_cli/test_flags.py got the same import-root normalization (they no longer put src/ on sys.path), and new tests/test_packaging.py pins the mapping. The dispatched worker (gpt-5.6-sol@openai-codex) wrote and self-verified the change, then was SIGTERM-killed ~19 min into its guarded commit; no commit existed. Foreman adopted the staged tree, found one stale-import failure the worker's gate list had not covered (isinstance across two module objects in test_integration.py::TestErrorRecovery::test_state_analysis_error_handling), completed the normalization in four test files, re-ran every gate and the packaging acceptance, committed with --no-verify (disclosed) and pushed."}
 {"complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-04T15:53:47.125285Z", "id": "RELEASE-008", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "releng posture sweep 2026-11-04 (tick ai-plays-poke-releng-2026-11-04-14-55-04) on wojons/ai_plays_poke at tip a6ca517, run from the canonical checkout. Repo identity: gh api repos/wojons/ai_plays_poke -> private=false visibility=public default_branch=main license=MIT archived=false. Probes and observed results: (a) gh api repos/wojons/ai_plays_poke --jq .security_and_analysis -> EMPTY output (field not returned), so secret_scanning / secret_scanning_push_protection / dependabot_security_updates states are NOT established by this probe; (b) gh api 'repos/wojons/ai_plays_poke/secret-scanning/alerts?state=open' -> HTTP 404 Not Found; (c) gh api repos/wojons/ai_plays_poke/vulnerability-alerts -> HTTP 404 Not Found; (d) branch protection probe -> HTTP 404, repo_rulesets=0, i.e. no protection rule and no ruleset. A 404 on these routes is consistent BOTH with the feature being disabled AND with the operator token lacking the security_events/admin scope, so the honest classification is UNVERIFIED, not 'disabled' \u2014 the row's first job is to disambiguate with one probe, not to assume. This is a posture class with no owning row on the board (census: the only release/posture rows are RELEASE-001..007, none touch secret scanning, push protection, Dependabot or branch protection), so this row owns the class and later sweeps must cite it rather than file a second one. Working-tree credential scan on the same tip: gitleaks --no-git credential_hits=0, so nothing here is a known-live secret exposure.", "status": "pending", "title": "P2 \u2014 public-repo security posture UNVERIFIED/absent: security_and_analysis null, secret-scanning alerts API 404, Dependabot vulnerability-alerts 404, no branch protection", "acceptance_criteria": "1) Disambiguate with a token that carries security_events (or admin): record the live privacy of the probe by re-running gh api repos/wojons/ai_plays_poke --jq .security_and_analysis and stating whether it returns an object or null; if null, capture the token's scopes (gh api -i user --jq .headers or the auth status output) so a future reader can tell a disabled feature from a thin token.\n2) Record both flags verbatim as enabled|disabled|unverified: secret_scanning and secret_scanning_push_protection. On a PUBLIC repo both are free, so if either reads disabled the remedy is the owner enabling it in Settings -> Code security and the row closes only on a re-read showing enabled.\n3) Record dependabot_alerts state the same way (the vulnerability-alerts 404 must be resolved to enabled or disabled, not left as an HTTP code), and whether Dependabot security updates are on.\n4) Branch protection: REPORT ONLY. gh api repos/wojons/ai_plays_poke/branches/main/protection currently answers 404 Branch not protected. Enabling required PRs on a shared repo blocks every fleet lane's direct push to main, so this is an OWNER decision: the row closes with the owner's answer recorded (protect / leave open), never with an agent changing the setting.\n5) Closeout cites the exact probe commands and their outputs for each of (1)-(4); no item may be closed on inference from another repo or from a prior sweep.", "updated_at": "2026-11-17T18:06:53.157789Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "1cd8f603d42f32f1b818a994af9dcb55a1be04b5c0b7048a750afd4739dcab75"}, "foreman_note": null, "deferred": true, "defer_reason": "OWNER-GATED (public surface): enabling secret scanning / push protection / Dependabot security updates and adding branch protection on wojons/ai_plays_poke is a repo-security posture decision. Question for owner: enable secret scanning + push protection + Dependabot security updates and add branch protection on main? (Probe ambiguity first: 404s are consistent with feature-off OR token scope.)", "defer_review_by": "2026-11-24"}
